must be true for any integers $x$ and $y?$\n\n- $6$ divides $(24x+30y)$\n- $3$ divides $(24x+30y)$\n- $5$ divides $(24x+30y)$" 13194139533543 17592186045585 true] [17592186407537 1072 #uuid "e7df593d-9767-5ee4-9c1c-cf41d12d4aeb" 13194139533543 17592186045585 true] [17592186407537 1074 "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n24x+30y=6(4x+5y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $4x+5y$ must be an integer, too. So, $6$ divides $(24x+30y).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n24x+30y=3(8x+10y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $8x+10y$ must be an integer, too. So, $3$ divides $(24x+30y).$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, if $x=-1$ and $y=1,$ we have $24(-1)+30(1)=6,$ which is not divisible by $5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" I and II only.\"" 13194139533543 17592186045585 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0341c354-0b34-5253-835d-01bf5f74e9d3" 17592186407370 "answer-046494f7-4180-59bc-84aa-9b1496ae4ecb" 17592186407371 "answer-0494a0c4-3cbc-5304-8920-956b6740222b" 17592186407372 "answer-070efb65-293c-5069-a098-e98293361bfb" 17592186407373 "answer-077fe147-bb8c-5245-adec-2f208cac3d00" 17592186407374 "answer-0c0b9dc9-474b-5e1b-9fc4-be003d4dfe59" 17592186407375 "answer-103cb213-0ae1-5f15-9c55-1cc6e3d17f17" 17592186407376 "answer-120145e5-ce36-5d3e-8425-5ff89fa57186" 17592186407377 "answer-1278745e-9ac1-5d09-b721-84a234f65b51" 17592186407378 "answer-135d7da1-4d43-56cc-931b-0e7278c9cb21" 17592186407379 "answer-1370f713-1610-576a-bf8c-3f77dcb87ae3" 17592186407380 "answer-14b34004-b613-54e3-9703-eedc75a5ef13" 17592186407381 "answer-19ee153e-bbda-569b-b725-6b0e9fe9f456" 17592186407382 "answer-1a0dedd9-4f67-524e-9daf-f07c1261bfad" 17592186407383 "answer-1ae5e5a6-de77-5fe1-b73c-0bef11fa3